@startuml
!theme plain
skinparam backgroundColor #FAFCFE
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontName SansSerif
skinparam componentStyle rectangle
skinparam ArrowColor #365369
skinparam packageBorderColor #849CAD
skinparam componentBackgroundColor #EAF4FA
skinparam noteBackgroundColor #FFF6D7
left to right direction

title Login HUD — presentation and shutdown authorization

actor User
package "GNOME Shell 46 / Wayland" {
  component "Native end-session dialog" as Native
  component "Login HUD extension\ncurrent-session validation\nprogress / reports / cancellation" as HUD
  component "Shell chrome\nstartup: bounded input region\nshutdown: conditional modal grab" as UI
}
package "Private per-user files" {
  artifact "login-hud-status.json\noperation context + stages" as Status
  artifact "request → rendered → commit\ncancel / prepared markers" as Markers
  artifact "alerts.json\ngc-profiled/status.json" as Reports
}
package "Separate producers" {
  component "Workspace coordinator\noperation ownership\ncheckpoint verification / recovery" as Coordinator
  component "Application restore / capture adapters" as Adapters
  component "Owned-system collector\nand cleanup scheduler" as Collectors
}

User --> Native : confirms Power Off / Restart
Native --> HUD : final confirmation interception
HUD --> UI : render validated state
User --> UI : expand / review / cancel
Coordinator --> Status : atomic replacement
Status --> HUD : directory monitor + validation
HUD --> Markers : request / painted / commit / cancel
Markers --> Coordinator : exact operation-bound evidence
Coordinator --> Markers : prepared / recovery result
Markers --> HUD : matching prepared proof
HUD --> Native : saved confirmation\nonly after proof
Coordinator --> Adapters : restore / verify / checkpoint
Collectors --> Reports : bounded status reports
Reports --> HUD : startup tabs only

note bottom of HUD
No application restoration or cleanup policy here.
Startup never acquires a modal grab.
Missing, stale or mismatched evidence cannot
 authorize a shutdown handoff.
end note
@enduml
